# Jak 3: the menu pointer on the title's menu (LIST-0.1.1 item 19), as tests/jak2_ptr_menu.sim. A first boot plays the
# opening (Y skips it to the title), A opens the title's menu; the right hand turns from high to low, a shot at each
# height (the row under the dot is picked), then the dot back on the lowest row (Quit, at 7 degrees: the middle of its
# bar; at 0 the dot is under the menu, where the trigger picks nothing, sim b37 ptr3) and the trigger: its Yes / No
# footer. Then at 4, 0 and -4 degrees the dot to the left half (12 degrees: Yes) and the right half (-4: No), a shot
# each (JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1 logs the dot against the footer's middle), and last the trigger on No at 4 degrees, which
# closes the question (a click on Yes would quit the game). Sim b38: the footer's middle at y 290.8 of the game's
# screen, the dot on it at 4 degrees (y 293.5), the highlight following it to Yes and No; at 0 the dot is under the
# question's bar (y 323.6) and a click there finds no row.
